From: 6Xkljk8Vj7Tk1k4 <6Xkljk8Vj7Tk1k4@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 18:48:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] gta4xl-common: Include the LineageOS libperfmgr sepolicy

The Pixel power HAL (android.hardware.power-service.pixel-libperfmgr)
starts a ThermalStateListener from its init thread that looks up
android.hardware.thermal.IThermal/default and registers a throttling
callback (aidl/utils/ThermalStateListener.cpp), but hal_power_default is
not a hal_thermal client here:

  avc: denied { find } for pid=4840 uid=0
  name=android.hardware.thermal.IThermal/default
  scontext=u:r:hal_power_default:s0 tcontext=u:object_r:hal_thermal_service:s0
  tclass=service_manager permissive=0

waitForService() returns null, the listener logs "Cannot get Thermal
Hal binder!" and keeps ThrottlingSeverity::NONE. That value is only
consumed by the ADPF session-metrics collection (PowerSessionManager,
gated on EnableMetricCollection in powerhint.json, which this device
does not set), so hints, boosts and ADPF sessions are unaffected - the
denial is log noise. It was already present on the lineage-23.2
baseline, together with a fwk_stats_service find denial from the same
HAL.

device/lineage/sepolicy/libperfmgr is LineageOS' policy module for
devices running the Pixel libperfmgr power HAL: it carries
hal_client_domain(hal_power_default, hal_thermal), the IStats find
rule, and labels vendor.powerhal.* as vendor_power_prop (today those
props fall into vendor_default_prop). Include it like the exynos and
libion modules.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 BoardConfigCommon.mk | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/BoardConfigCommon.mk b/BoardConfigCommon.mk
index 180dd4e..5e0e182 100644
--- a/BoardConfigCommon.mk
+++ b/BoardConfigCommon.mk
@@ -165,6 +165,7 @@ VENDOR_SECURITY_PATCH := 2024-05-01
 BOARD_SEPOLICY_TEE_FLAVOR := teegris
 include device/lineage/sepolicy/exynos/sepolicy.mk
 include device/lineage/sepolicy/libion/sepolicy.mk
+include device/lineage/sepolicy/libperfmgr/sepolicy.mk
 include device/samsung_slsi/sepolicy/sepolicy.mk
 
 BOARD_VENDOR_SEPOLICY_DIRS += $(COMMON_PATH)/sepolicy/vendor
